menu "Needle"

config NEEDLE_WEB_UI
    bool "Serve the built-in web demo"
    default y
    help
        Embed the demo page, its tokenizer and the 8192-entry vocabulary into
        the app image (about 72 KB gzipped) and serve them from "/".

        Leave this on for the out-of-the-box experience: flash the board, open
        its address, ask it something.

        Turn it off for an API-only build. The board still answers
        POST /api/tokens and GET /api/status, and it still runs the model; it
        just stops serving a front end. Clients tokenize on their side, which
        is what demos/ shows.

endmenu
